---
import Docs from '../layouts/Docs.astro';
import Guides from '../components/Guides.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import { ddTheme } from '../lib/syntax';
import { base } from '../lib/nav';
import skill from '../../skill/dawn-and-dusk/SKILL.md?raw';

const install = `# From a clone of this repository: install into one project
npm run skill:install -- ~/code/my-app
# → ~/code/my-app/.claude/skills/dawn-and-dusk (replaced if it's already there)

# Without a clone: run this inside the project (evals/ is for developing the skill, so it goes)
npx degit cxkw-dev/dawn-and-dusk/skill/dawn-and-dusk .claude/skills/dawn-and-dusk && rm -rf .claude/skills/dawn-and-dusk/evals`;

const agentsMd = `## UI: dawn & dusk design system
- Copy dawn-and-dusk.css, dawn-and-dusk.js and icons.svg from github.com/cxkw-dev/dawn-and-dusk/tree/main/release.
  Load the CSS and JS once; paste icons.svg once after <body>.
- Build with semantic HTML + dd- classes; style only with var(--dd-*) tokens. Never hard-code colours.
- Tone, not borders: --dd-bg → --dd-surface → --dd-surface-2. Shadows only on floating layers.
- One .dd-btn--primary per view. Headings: .dd-h1/.dd-h2 (lowercase lockup). Data in .dd-mono.
- Component catalogue: https://cxkw-dev.github.io/dawn-and-dusk — check dawn and dusk before finishing.`;
---
<Docs title="Agent skill" group="AI" lead="Hand dawn & dusk to an AI agent. The skill teaches it the tokens, the rules and every component, and ships the CSS, JS and icons it needs.">
  <p>The skill is optional. To use the components in your app, start with the <a href={`${base}/getting-started`}>installation guide and starters</a>.</p>
  <h2 id="whats-inside">What’s inside</h2>
  <div class="doc-cards">
    <div class="doc-card"><b>SKILL.md</b><span>When to use the system, how to install it into a project, and the rules that make it look right.</span></div>
    <div class="doc-card"><b>references/components/</b><span>One file per component with the exact markup of every docs example, its classes and guidelines. Generated from these docs.</span></div>
    <div class="doc-card"><b>references/components.md</b><span>Every component’s classes, <code>data-dd-*</code> hooks and behaviours in one file. Generated from <code>ds/</code>.</span></div>
    <div class="doc-card"><b>references/tokens.md</b><span>Every token with its dawn and dusk value, the base classes and every icon name. Generated from <code>ds/</code>.</span></div>
    <div class="doc-card"><b>references/patterns.md</b><span>Page recipes: dashboard, data explorer, settings, landing and pricing.</span></div>
    <div class="doc-card"><b>references/frameworks.md</b><span>React, Next.js, Vue, Svelte and Astro, theming without a flash, and living next to Tailwind.</span></div>
    <div class="doc-card"><b>assets/</b><span><code>dawn-and-dusk.css</code>, <code>dawn-and-dusk.js</code>, <code>tokens.css</code> and <code>icons.svg</code>, ready to copy into a project.</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="install">Install for Claude</h2>
  <p>Install the skill into each project that uses dawn & dusk, never into your global <code>~/.claude/skills</code>: other projects, such as client work, keep their own design language. Claude Code finds it in the project’s <code>.claude/skills</code> folder and uses it whenever you ask for UI there. Commit the folder so teammates get it too.</p>
  <Code code={install} lang="bash" theme={ddTheme} wrap />
  <p>In the Claude apps, zip the <code>skill/dawn-and-dusk</code> folder (leave out <code>evals/</code>) and upload it as a custom skill. Its description limits it to dawn & dusk work.</p>

  <h2 id="other-agents">Other agents</h2>
  <p>Agents without skill support (Cursor, Copilot, Codex…) get most of the way with a short block in <code>AGENTS.md</code> or the system prompt, plus the release files:</p>
  <Code code={agentsMd} lang="markdown" theme={ddTheme} wrap />

  <h2 id="keeping-in-sync">Keeping it in sync</h2>
  <p>The references are generated, so the skill can’t describe a component that doesn’t exist. <code>npm run build:ds</code> refreshes the assets, <code>tokens.md</code> and <code>components.md</code> from <code>ds/</code>; <code>npm run build</code> also regenerates the per-component markup from the built docs. Run <code>npm run skill:install</code> again to update a project’s copy.</p>

  <h2 id="skill-md">SKILL.md</h2>
  <Code code={skill} lang="markdown" theme={ddTheme} wrap />

  <h2 id="guidelines">Prompting tips</h2>
  <Guides do={['Name the page type: “a dawn & dusk dashboard for deploy health”.', 'Ask the agent to check dusk and a phone width before it finishes.', 'Point it at a component page when you want a specific variant.']} dont={['Don’t paste raw hex values into prompts; ask for tokens.', 'Don’t let it add a second CSS framework next to dawn & dusk.']} />
</Docs>
